# core.autocrlf=true on Windows rewrites checked-out files to CRLF. For files
# that are served verbatim to third-party validators, that corrupts the bytes
# they check, so pin them to LF.
# ads.txt must be a byte-for-byte mirror of Ezoic's Ads.txt Manager output,
# which uses CRLF. Treat it as binary so git never rewrites its line endings.
public/ads.txt   -text

public/robots.txt text eol=lf
public/sitemap.xml text eol=lf
